<title>USA: OHSL Financial Q3 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>OHSL Financial Q3 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>OHSL FINANCIAL CORP</p>
<p>					    Three months ended Sept 30:</p>
<p> CONSOLIDATED RESULTS OF OPERATIONS	  1996	    1995</p>
<p>							 (000)	  (000)</p>
<p> Interest income				   4,109	  3,836</p>
<p> Interest expense				  2,407	  2,185</p>
<p> Net interest income			     1,702	  1,651</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses			 (2)		3</p>
<p> Net interest income after provision	 1,704	  1,648</p>
<p> Noninterest income				   97	    150</p>
<p> Noninterest expense			     2,105	    993</p>
<p> Net income before tax provision	     (304)	    805</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes		    (102)	    269</p>
<p> Net income					  (202)	    536</p>
<p> EARNINGS (LOSS) PER SHARE		   ($0.16)	  $0.43</p>
<p> BOOK VALUE PER SHARE (END OF PERIOD)	20.58	  20.53</p>
<p>					     Nine months ended Sept 30:</p>
<p> CONSOLIDATED RESULTS OF OPERATIONS	  1996	    1995</p>
<p>							 (000)	  (000)</p>
<p> Interest income				  12,024	 10,816</p>
<p> Interest expense				  6,876	  6,001</p>
<p> Net interest income			     5,148	  4,815</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses			   2		7</p>
<p> Net interest income after provision	 5,146	  4,808</p>
<p> Noninterest income				  251	    365</p>
<p> Noninterest expense			     4,269	  3,029</p>
<p> Net income before tax provision	     1,128	  2,144</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			397	    733</p>
<p> Net income					    731	  1,411</p>
<p> EARNINGS PER SHARE				$0.58	  $1.12</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 1996 includes a &quot;special assessment&quot; for the recapitalization of the Savings Association Insurance Fund (&quot;SAIF&quot;), which was signed into law on September 30. OHSL's charge for this special assessment was $927,000, resulting in an after-tax charge of $612,000.  Without this one-time assessment, OHSL would have reported net income for the quarter ended September 30, 1996 of $410,000.</p>
